{
  "title": "🔄 Converting One Solid to Another — Volume Stays Constant!",
  "hook": "A metallic sphere is melted and recast into a cylinder. A cone-shaped clay model is reshaped into a sphere. In both cases, the VOLUME doesn't change — only the shape! This is the key insight.",
  "explanation": "<div style=\"background:#F5F5F5;border-left:3px solid #4A90D9;border-radius:6px;padding:8px 12px;margin:6px 0;font-size:0.9rem\"><b>Fundamental Rule:</b> When a solid is melted/reshaped into another solid, the <b>volume remains the same</b>.</div><p><b>Volume formulas you need:</b></p><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:12px 0;font-size:0.88rem\"><tr><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Solid</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Volume</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Surface Area</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Cube (side a)</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">a³</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">6a²</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Cuboid (l×b×h)</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">lbh</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">2(lb + bh + hl)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Cylinder (r, h)</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">πr²h</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">2πr(r + h)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Cone (r, h, l)</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">⅓πr²h</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">πr(r + l)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Sphere (r)</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">⁴⁄₃πr³</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">4πr²</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Hemisphere (r)</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">⅔πr³</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">3πr²</td></tr></table><div style=\"margin:12px 0\"><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#1565C0;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">1</div><div><strong>Write volume of original solid</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\"></span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#1565C0;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">2</div><div><strong>Write volume of new solid (in terms of unknowns)</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\"></span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#1565C0;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">3</div><div><strong>Set them equal</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">Volume₁ = Volume₂</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#1565C0;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">4</div><div><strong>Solve for the unknown dimension</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\"></span></div></div></div><div style=\"background:#FFF8E1;border-left:4px solid #FFB300;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 14px;margin:10px 0;font-size:0.88rem\">💡 <strong>Tip:</strong> If the original is split into many smaller solids: Volume of original = n × Volume of each small solid.</div>",
  "worked_example": "<b>Example:</b> A metallic sphere of radius 6 cm is melted and recast into a cylinder of radius 4 cm. Find the height.<br><br><div style=\"margin:12px 0\"><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">1</div><div><strong>Volume of sphere</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">V = (4/3)π(6)³ = (4/3)π(216) = 288π cm³</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">2</div><div><strong>Volume of cylinder</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">V = π(4)²h = 16πh cm³</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">3</div><div><strong>Set equal</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">16πh = 288π → h = 18 cm</span></div></div></div>",
  "try_this": {
    "question": "A cone of radius 3 cm and height 8 cm is melted into a sphere. Find the radius of the sphere.",
    "hint": "Volume of cone = ⅓πr²h. Volume of sphere = ⁴⁄₃πR³. Set equal and solve.",
    "answer": "(1/3)π(9)(8) = (4/3)πR³. 24π = (4/3)πR³. R³ = 18. R = ∛18 ≈ 2.62 cm."
  },
  "fun_fact": "Archimedes discovered that a sphere fits perfectly inside a cylinder of the same height and diameter — and the sphere's volume is exactly 2/3 of the cylinder's!"
